The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says that all its reports are one issue. The desk's own
rule says otherwise. `fingerprint.ts` puts two reports in one issue only when they come from the
same place and carry the same server code. The place is the product that the reporter's tenant
runs, not the tag that intake chose at night. Run over the reports in #4471, that rule gives this:

<IssueTickets ticket={4471} />

<Callout kind="warn">

Change #29 fixed the `sched-prod` issue. The `tram-3` and `rota-6` reports were closed with #4471,
so they had no ticket and nobody followed up. With a ticket each, engineering answered: change #31
fixed the `rota-6` sync, and `tram-3` is won't fix, because the boards are retired.

</Callout>

## Why these are separate issues

- **Same code, other place.** `tram-3` and `sched-prod` both raise `E-TZ-114`. The departure
  boards and the shift app are different products, so the desk counts them as different bugs.
- **Another code.** `rota-6` raises `E-SYNC-04`. Care homes see the night shift twice, one hour
  apart. That is a sync fault, not a moved shift.
- **Intake tags are a guess.** Some reports were tagged `sched-prod` at night. The reporter's
  tenant puts them in `tram-3` (Metro Lund also mails from `ml-trafik.se`) and in `rota-6`
  (phone calls from care homes). The "tagged as" column on the [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471)
  shows them.
- **Client codes are not issues.** Some reports also quote `E-UI-31` or `E-NET-03`. That is the
  app that complains on the way down. Each of those reports also carries a server code.
- **Copies count once.** The export has some rows twice. The tables count each report id once.

## The 03:12 row

One row in the `sched-prod` group is not a report. `R-41200` has no reporter, no subject and no
source. Its body is the 03:12 job's own result line: it says `clean` and carries `E-TZ-114`. It
came before the first customer wrote in. Read it as the first sign of the night, not as a person.
The engineers who own the job should find out why a run that raised `E-TZ-114` reported clean.

## For the desk

- Open one ticket per issue, as the table above does. Merge on place and server code, not on
  the subject line.
- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) and the
  [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) still say "merge on subject". They are stale. A new decision
  record should replace 0001; 0001 itself stays as it is.

